### 2026-08-16T01:49:56.879Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

All 5 parts of the Melody scrubber redesign are implemented, tested, and committed (`[REDACTED_SECRET]`):

1. **Real I-beam marker** — CSS-drawn stem + serifs, replacing the `▾` glyph.
2. **Uniform spacing** — real flex+gap layout, dropped the asymmetric `" - "` text-node separators.
3. **Full-song scrollable timeline** — real songs render every note up front with edge-scroll while dragging; Random stays exactly as before (explicitly tested).
4. **Measure ticks** — `parseMIDI` now returns effective BPM; two independent 120bpm literals hoisted into one shared constant.
5. **Spaced-repetition auto-advance** — 3 clean playthroughs advances the drilled segment a full measure, reset by a mistake/scrub/new-song-load, survives mode switches per INV-48.

Along the way I caught and fixed two real bugs before they shipped: a negative `marker.style.left` that made the marker unclickable on the first note (caught by the drag tests going red), and an auto-advance clamp that could strand `startIndex` back inside the same measure instead of growing `targetLength` to cover the new segment (caught by a red/green check before finalizing). Full desktop, invariants (Mobile + Tablet Chrome), and mobile suites pass except the two pre-existing unrelated flakes already known from earlier this session (Blast's landscape-queue test, and one INV-23 timing flake that passed on retry).


