Both bugs are fixed and committed (`[REDACTED_SECRET]`):

1. **Save downgrading to a download** — the folder picker/permission calls only ever requested `'read'`, never `'readwrite'`, so `saveFileAs`'s write threw silently and fell back to a browser download. Now requests `'readwrite'` throughout; if you'd already granted the folder under the old read-only default, you'll see the existing "Reconnect Folder" prompt once to re-grant it.
2. **Stale dropdown after moving files** — the listing only refreshed at four fixed moments (restore/reconnect/choose-folder/post-save), never on opening the dropdown. It now re-lists in the background when you click/focus the dropdown — best-effort, since a native `<select>` can't wait on an async refresh before it paints, so the very next open may still show the old list, but the one after that will be current.

Both bugs live in the shared `js/file-folder.js` code, so this fixes Melody/Compose's folder too, not just Life's. Full desktop suite (124) and invariants (59 on Mobile Chrome) pass.


