- **Bundled songs, as MusicXML**: key signature and time signature are already in the file — an author wrote them down. Zero inference needed, for any of the three.
- **Compose**: rather than inferring a key/time-signature from what got tapped, make it an explicit setting (same shape as the existing tempo/subdivision controls) — sidesteps spelling and measure inference entirely for anything composed here.
- **MIDI uploads and Random**: the only genuinely raw-performance-data sources left — nothing authored, so this is the one place all three problems are real and unavoidable. This was already the scope for rhythm quantization; now it's also where spelling and measure-inference quality actually matters.

