### 2026-08-17T02:38:30.037Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Good exercise — [REDACTED_PRIVATE_INFO]

## Supported (planned)

| Feature | Notes |
|---|---|
| Pitch (step/alter/octave) | The whole point — MIDI↔pitch already exists via `Tonnetz.getMidi`/`getNoteName`; enharmonic spelling per key sig is the piece just discussed |
| Duration / note values (whole–16th, dotted) | Core to the staff display and Compose editing |
| Rests | Needed to represent gaps between notes |
| Key signature, incl. mid-piece changes | Just designed — a `{time, key}` track, Compose can insert changes |
| Time signature, incl. mid-piece changes | Same track mechanism as key |
| Measures / barlines | The explicit "bar spans everything" requirement |
| Tempo | Already have `state.tempo`; MusicXML's `<sound tempo>`/`<metronome>` maps directly |
| Grand staff (one part, two staves split by register) | What was designed — a *register split* of one monophonic line, not genuine independent-hands piano writing |
| Chords (simultaneous notes) | Compose's existing `flushChordBuffer` already records true simultaneous notes — maps onto MusicXML's `<chord/>` marker within one voice |

## Explicitly excluded

| Feature | Why |
|---|---|
| Multiple parts/instruments | Tonncade is one Tonnetz, one voice, by its whole nature |
| Multiple independent voices per staff (polyphony) | Note model is a flat monophonic sequence (+ chords, above) — no independent voice lines |
| Guitar tab, percussion/unpitched notation | Not relevant to a pitched hex-lattice app |
| Lyrics (`<lyric>`) | Gameplay is instrumental note-matching; a file's actual sung words, if present, get ignored |
| Dynamics, articulations, ornaments, technical marks (fingering etc.) | Performance nuance — nothing in this app's model checks or sonifies per-note dynamics/articulation today |
| Chord symbols (`<harmony>`, e.g. "Cmaj7" chart annotations) | Not part of the current design |
| Grace notes, tremolo, glissando | Beyond the "simple diatonic tapped melody" scope already agreed on |
| Page layout/engraving directives (margins, breaks, fonts) | No print output, in-browser only |
| Cross-staff notation, manual beam/stem overrides | Left to VexFlow's default engraving |
| Transposing instruments (`<transpose>`) | Concert pitch only, matches the existing "true pitch" invariant (INV-46) |

## Worth a real decision, not a clean yes/no

- **Repeat signs / voltas / D.C./D.S.** — a MusicXML with a repeat bar would currently just be read linearly, once through, silently *not* expanding the repeat. This is a real, likely-to-be-hit gap (most real folk tunes have a repeat sign) with a genuinely confusing failure mode (practicing a "shorter" song than the real one, with no error). Worth explicitly deciding: silently flatten (current default), warn, or actually expand repeats into the linear note sequence at import time (bounded, doable — repeat barlines are a well-defined structure).
- **Ties** — not just cosmetic. Whenever quantized duration doesn't fit a single notatable value, or a note should sustain across a barline, correct notation needs a tie curve connecting two noteheads of the same pitch. Excluding ties means such a note renders as two unconnected same-pitch noteheads back-to-back — plausibly misread as two separate notes rather than one held one. Worth explicitly deciding whether v1 emits ties (real, bounded work — detect "duration crosses boundary or isn't a single legal value," split, tie) or accepts that visual ambiguity for now.
- **Compressed MusicXML (`.mxl`)** — most real notation software (MuseScore, Finale, etc.) exports `.mxl` (a zip container) by default, not plain `.musicxml`/`.xml`. This directly affects the "professional exports their own file and uploads it" escape hatch the whole music21-avoidance argument leans on — if we only parse plain XML text, that path silently fails for anyone whose tool defaults to `.mxl`. Needs deciding: support unzipping on upload (a small, well-defined addition — it's just a zip container), or document "export uncompressed XML" as a requirement.

Want any of those three folded into the doc as open items, or decided now?


